new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6858174
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/subset-selector/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# ClamAV 1.5.4 Legal Redress backport
+
+This is a custom, locally validated backport onto official tag `clamav-1.5.4`.
+It is **experimental, not a production release approval**. The official release
+baseline includes that tag's security fixes; the modifications are not vendor-certified.
+See [validation and limitations](../../docs/legal-redress-backport.md).
+
+**Compatibility limit:** synthetic first-hit selection can differ from unmodified
+ClamAV, including weak/strong selection on stable. All-match detection contracts
+pass; alert order and final selected names can differ. See the report for scope.
+
+Full database mode remains the default. Opt in with
+**`--database-profile=legal-redress`** on this adapter's `scan.py` or `intake.py`.
+This flag is not added to upstream `clamscan` or `clamd`. The reduced profile forces
+accepting all-match scanning; no-detection candidates stay held. Originals, prior
+findings, signed database inputs and the separate complaint narrative are preserved.
+
+## Build and configure
+
+Use ClamAV's release build dependencies plus Python 3.10+, json-c/OpenSSL development
+headers and pkg-config. Pillow is needed for the boundary fixtures. Build from this
+source directory with a supported C/Rust toolchain:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B ../build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DENABLE_TESTS=ON -DENABLE_UNRAR=ON -DENABLE_MILTER=OFF \
+  -DENABLE_CLAMONACC=OFF -DENABLE_MAN_PAGES=OFF
+cmake --build ../build -j2
+python3 tools/subset-selector/build_probe.py --build ../build --output ../scan_probe
+export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$(realpath ../build/libclamav):$(realpath ../build/libclamunrar_iface):$(realpath ../build/libclamunrar)${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
+python3 tools/subset-selector/select_db.py \
+  --lib ../build/libclamav/libclamav.so.12.1.0 --probe ../scan_probe \
+  --certs certs --output ../generation-001 \
+  /private/signed/main.cvd /private/signed/daily.cvd /private/signed/bytecode.cvd
+python3 tools/subset-selector/intake.py \
+  --database-profile=legal-redress \
+  --source /private/upload/original.pdf --quarantine /private/quarantine \
+  --generation ../generation-001 --probe ../scan_probe \
+  --lib ../build/libclamav/libclamav.so.12.1.0 --certs certs
+```
+
+Set full mode by omitting the profile flag or using `--database-profile=full`.
+`scan.py` also supports `--database /private/signed-dbs` for full-only scanning
+without a selector generation. Intake uses a verified generation in either mode.
+Generations are bound to the exact engine, probe, selector and profile: regenerate
+when any changes. Generation output must not exist. Keep inputs and parent directories
+service-owned and immutable to upload users. Never disable signature verification.
+
+Full-load validation runs during preparation and needs a separate worker with full
+engine memory. The reduced scan flag never runs that full-load validation child.
+The old 303 MiB discussion is not a memory cap or a measurement of these backports.
+The adapter exposes `--reload-overlap` for diagnostics; production limits must be
+measured on the deployment host with its actual workload and concurrency.
+
+The stable build uses the modern scan/layer API and retains the borrowed-key Rust evidence optimization.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+ctest --test-dir ../build -R '^(libclamav|libclamav_rust|clamscan|sigtool)$' --output-on-failure
+python3 tools/subset-selector/test_selector.py
+python3 tools/subset-selector/test_configuration.py
+python3 tools/subset-selector/test_hardening.py
+```
+
+Run the independently instrumented [boundary test](boundary/README.md), then
+`test_flags.py` against a probe built with an unmodified copy of the same release.
+The report records the 138-file corpus and exact commands. Stable uses
+`test_integration.py --require-detections`; LTS uses `test_legacy_integration.py`
+with a same-release original probe. The modern callback override/severity tests
+cannot be run against the LTS API. Both run signed-input and real intake tests.
+
+Intake exits 0 clean / 1 detected / 2 failed / 3 held. The native diagnostic probe
+exits 0 when execution completes; each scan record must be inspected. Hardened
+intake rejects malformed output, verifies original hashes, preserves assessment
+history, serializes scanners per quarantine root and bounds resource use. Defaults:
+100 MiB source size, 180s wall time, 120s CPU, 2048 MiB virtual address space,
+48-hour daily database age. These are not a hostile-parser sandbox or a global
+cgroup RSS limit. Native scanning needs separate-principal/read-only evidence
+isolation, target-host recovery and update qualification before production use.
